  "description": "Blindness filter word lists and patterns (SPEC.md Principle 7, M4). All matching is case-insensitive. Terms in always_refuse_terms refuse a query or fact on their own. Terms in quantity_terms refuse only together with an event_terms hit or a measurement_pattern hit (so reference sizes like spacesuit height stay allowed). pronoun_terms work the same way: a quantity term plus a pronoun (he, they, it, ...) means the query asks about the filmed subject's own quantities. generative_terms refuse on their own (deepfakes, AI video); generative_patterns refuse model names (Sora, Veo, ...) and 'generated' only with generative context, so reference uses ('Sora rail bird', 'how is electricity generated') stay allowed. event_name_patterns refuse stunt/event framings (wall run, vertical wall, Red Bull + action) but not bare places or brands. feasibility_patterns refuse only together with a feasibility_action_terms hit, so verdict-seeking questions ('is it possible to run up a wall') are refused while plain references stay allowed. Regex lists use Python re syntax.",
